WEBVTT

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:45.940
<b>New Year's Envelopes Are 
Perfect for Dirty Jokes</b>

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.500
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose</b>

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.630
Gin-chan, Gin-chan.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.000
Give me my New Year's envelope!

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.610
Give me my New Year's envelope.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.880
New Year's envelope—

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.600
Where did you pick up that nasty habit?

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:26.110
A young lady shouldn't 
be begging for money.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.400
But everyone else was doing it.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.020
They said that grown-ups
on Earth somewhere

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.660
are supposed to give us New Year's envelopes.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:36.820
Hey, Gin-chan.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.910
What's inside a New Year's envelope?

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.860
Hey, give me a New Year's envelope!

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.920
Are you sure you want one?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.260
Yup. I don't know what a New Year's 
envelope is, but it's free.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.220
You won't regret your decision?

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:56.290
Huh?

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:02.530
Are you prepared to accept 
a New Year's envelope,

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.190
no matter what may happen?

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.850
Don't scare me.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:07.070
It can't be that big a deal.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.070
Gin-chan?

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:14.950
Gin-chan...?

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.500
Gin-chan!

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.490
Are you okay, Gin-chan?!

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.840
Hang in there!

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.130
What... What's wrong?

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.350
Gin-chan!

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.640
Take these...

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:48.590
Th-They were inside my 
New Year's envelope.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:50.990
Gin-chan!

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.730
G-Gin-chan, what are these?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.620
What is a New Year's 
envelope supposed to be?!

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:06.000
H-Have I taken something very, 
very important from you?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.630
I-It's okay...

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.690
I always knew this day would come.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.540
To be honest, I was always afraid.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:20.470
Afraid that you would ask 
for a New Year's envelope...

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.650
That our lives would fall apart...

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:27.410
I-I'm sorry, Gin-chan.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.360
I had no idea!

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:32.500
I didn't realize New Year's 
envelopes were such a big deal!

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.840
I don't need one then!

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.770
I don't need these mochi balls!

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.700
So, Gin-chan...

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.840
Kagura, this is what happens when

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.070
you take a New Year's 
envelope from an adult.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.930
Gin-chan!

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:54.610
But you said that you wanted 
a New Year's envelope,

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.750
no matter what happened.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:01.090
In that case, you shouldn't look back.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.990
You must cross my dead body, 
the dead bodies of us adults.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:10.360
Kagura...

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.110
You must collect seven of those balls.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.880
Claim those bloody phantom jewels from

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.450
relatives around the world.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.530
If you collect seven, you'll 
receive the legendary treasure

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:25.540
that will grant the wish of any kid.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.080
The Treasure Balls.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:33.090
I know... I know you can 
make your wish come true.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:37.050
For my sake...

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.040
Gin-chan...

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.700
Gin-chan!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.140
In your dreams!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.640
Hey, what's a Treasure Ball?

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.130
You came up with that gross act

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:58.040
because you didn't want to give 
me a New Year's envelope?!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.070
This is the year of the 
dragon, not the pig!

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:03.110
O-Oh, you knew I was lying?

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:04.380
That's not nice of you.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.790
I was playing along to soften you 
up, but you took it way too far!

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.850
But now you understand 
how difficult it is

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.070
for grown-ups to provide 
New Year's envelopes.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:16.000
I can't understand why someone 
would spit out white balls

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.930
when someone asks for 
a New Year's envelope!

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.290
Don't blame me.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:23.460
I lost all my Treasure 
Balls to the other kids.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.930
You mean you lost them 
at a pachinko parlor!

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.490
No wonder I'm coughing up Treasure Balls.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.130
I also coughed up the Treasure 
Soup I had for breakfast.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.880
In that case, you should 
just give me everything!

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.280
Seriously, why are you fighting 
on the first day of a new year?

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.840
Happy New Year.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.780
Here you are, Kagura-chan.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.880
Huh? What's that?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.250
What? You're supposed to give people

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.040
New Year's envelopes on New Year's Day.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.040
<b>New Year's Envelope
Kagura-chan</b>

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.060
Oh, really?!

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.770
You're awesome, Shinpachi!

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.910
Nah, Sis told me to bring this to you.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:58.210
I see! Yay!

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:02.260
I didn't expect to 
receive one at this age.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:05.970
Well, I guess Sis still 
thinks I'm just a kid.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:09.650
But I hope I can grow up to be like her.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.340
An adult who has plenty 
of money to give to kids.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.720
That's right.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:18.130
I don't want to grow up to be an 
adult who coughs up white balls.

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:21.800
Yeah, I don't want to grow up 
to be an adult who hides indoors

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.990
because he doesn't want to 
give out New Year's envelopes.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:28.520
Hey! Don't think I can't hear you!

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.830
Why don't I get a New Year's envelope?!

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.080
That's no fair!

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.500
That's why you're mad?!

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:36.030
You need to grow up, Gin-san!

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:39.320
You're supposed to be handing out 
envelopes, not receiving them!

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:42.220
Can't you act like a leader for once?

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.600
What are you talking about, fools?

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.430
A real man never drops 
the ball, or his balls.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:56.180
Here, use this.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:58.240
Huh?

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:02.610
We knew you wouldn't have any money left,

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.240
so we saved some of our pay.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:08.490
You can use it to do 
something good for once.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.990
You need to give us a 
reason to feel proud

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.800
that you're our leader.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.150
You...

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:18.510
And you have to pay back 
every penny, with interest.

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:21.120
Thank you!

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.130
Then I'll go triple the money so 
I have enough to give everyone!

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.930
Gintoki-sama?

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.940
Happy New Year, Gintoki-sama.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:34.980
Tama-san!

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:38.760
Shinpachi-sama, Kagura-sama, 
happy New Year.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:41.030
Oh, happy New Year.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.280
Happy New Year.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.010
Oh, that's right.

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:47.080
Start by giving one to Tama, moron.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.160
Don't drop the ball.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.790
That's not funny!

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:53.190
Oh, that's right. Tama 
may look like an adult,

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:57.250
but she was created a short while 
ago, so she should get one?

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:02.380
Yes, it says on Wikipedia that 
I was born on August 16th, 2007.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.150
What's that? Wikipedia 
exists in this world?

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.830
It most certainly does.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.850
Then what does it say about the fact

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:11.550
that there are barely any 
Amanto-like Amanto showing up?

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.020
The new restrictions aren't helping,

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.090
and it's a pain in the ass to 
come up with new characters.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:15.890
That's what it says.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:17.560
It doesn't say that anywhere!

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:20.110
That came straight from 
the author himself!

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:24.420
Anyway, Tama is like a reverse 
Conan-kun, so give her an envelope.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:27.450
No, she looks like an adult, 
so she doesn't count.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.920
You can't reverse everything!

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.120
Let's go look for a real kid.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:36.360
If you're looking for a kid to give a 
New Year's envelope, there's one right here.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:38.880
Shut up. I don't need 
a catty hag nagging...

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:41.710
It's me, Tama-chan.

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.380
Mister, give me an envelope.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:44.630
Die!

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:52.520
I wanted a few more lines...

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:56.320
Tsk, Shinpachi looks more like
Tama-chan when crossdressing than you do!

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.620
That's why you snapped?!

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.060
You're probably right though!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:03.860
Oh, it's Gin-san!

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:06.350
What? Are you visiting 
everyone for New Year's?

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:07.490
Happy New Year!

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:10.220
Don't "happy New Year" me.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:12.590
In the manga, this chapter 
ran before New Year's,

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.390
and we're airing this episode in March.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.130
So you're trying to turn back the

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.470
clock so you can get 
a New Year's envelope.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:20.780
New Year's envelope?

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.340
From you, Gin-san?!

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:23.420
Hinowa!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:24.840
I know!

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.760
Close the Yoshiwara ceiling!

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:28.730
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.720
Emergency alert!

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:32.300
Tell all the residents 
to brace for impact!

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.400
All hands prepare for an aerial assault!

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.030
Aye, aye!

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:37.540
What do you expect to come falling down?!

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.260
Do you want me to kill you all?!

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.260
Th-That means...

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.440
I came all the way out here.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.760
Just take it.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.760
Y-Yay!

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:49.670
Gin-san came here to give 
me a New Year's envelope!

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.290
What happened? Are you dying?

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.320
Are you going to die?

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.330
Shut up! He's the only kid I could 
think of, so I had to come here!

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.010
Isn't that wonderful, Seita?

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:58.710
Yup!

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:01.350
Look at how happy he is.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.290
See? It's not a bad idea 
to be nice once in a while.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.240
Keep your mouth shut.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:05.210
Are you satisfied now?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.070
Sorry.

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:08.450
That's right.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:12.910
I also prepared a New Year's 
gift to show my appreciation.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:14.890
Shinpa-san, Kagura-chan,

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.970
please take these.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:17.980
Tsukuyo.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.440
Take whichever one you want.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.440
We discovered the golden rod and balls

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.450
in Hosen's safe the other day.

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:33.350
I received this golden 
piece as a New Year's gift!

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:34.680
Isn't it pretty?

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.950
Oh, what are you going to give me?

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.690
Something golden?

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.480
Gin-san will probably 
give you a silver rod.

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:43.540
Nah, probably a silver ball.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:47.590
I'll go buy some silver paint 
that's safe for your skin.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:49.720
Silver soul!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.540
Uh, what am I supposed to do?

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.080
What do you want me to do?

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.150
They're looking for golden balls.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.700
All I got are some sagging balls.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.780
That doesn't mean you should 
paint your balls silver.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.270
Make them stop sagging.

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:03.730
It doesn't work that way!

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:08.490
This trade would be like highway robbery!

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.370
It's the thought that counts.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.500
Then you go give them your thought!

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.470
Calm down. Just make them stop sagging.

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:16.370
I said that it doesn't work that way!

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:19.200
Uh, is something wrong, Gin-san?

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.160
No, you see...

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:23.210
Ahem.

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:28.420
I'll let you borrow this.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.050
Hand it to him.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.320
She's helping us!

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:35.090
She's letting us rent a golden bar!

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.810
I can't afford to borrow that!

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:40.570
I won't be able to pay you back!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.880
We're only letting you borrow 
this temporarily anyway.

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:45.060
I don't need it!

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:47.310
You think I can hand that 
over with a straight face?!

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.630
Stop trying to act tough!

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:52.190
Keep your voice down! He'll hear you!

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:55.500
It's your fault for refusing to take it!

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.010
You're talking out loud and 
covering up your coughing!

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:59.130
Hey!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.380
Gin-san, Tsukuyo-san!

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.580
We can hear everything you're saying!

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:06.250
Seita-kun's trying to pretend 
that he didn't see anything!

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:07.740
Fine.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.810
If you're gonna insist, I'll borrow it.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.260
Don't look at me.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.260
Where? Where is it?

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.160
Right here.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.960
The rod is right here.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:16.510
Rod?

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.550
No, it's lower.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.520
Rod? This is more like a ball.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:25.440
What do you think you're doing?!

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.460
G-Gin-san!

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:36.090
And there's your New Year's envelope.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:49.290
Are you going to keep 
coughing up white balls?

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:53.550
The last pair was half-digested.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:55.400
I won't be able to use that trick again.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.300
You never should have been 
able to use that trick.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.940
Let's just stop.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:02.150
This isn't my thing.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:06.060
I'm not the kind of person 
who hands out money.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.520
Let's just spend it on ourselves 
and go out on the town.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.560
It's on me.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.820
Don't spend our hard-earned 
money on yourself!

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:16.330
But there aren't any 
other kids in this show.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:19.230
All we got are a bunch of 
old men who act like kids.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:20.550
Nobody ever said that you

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.550
have to give New Year's 
envelopes to kids.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:24.080
You could give one to 
a younger colleague.

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.650
Colleague? I don't have any of those.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.790
<b>Gintoki-senpai!</b>

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:31.380
Hey, who was that?!

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.880
<b>Oh, it's Gintoki-senpai!</b>

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.880
Oh, Gintoki.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:38.080
Come over here. I just 
met a familiar face.

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.400
Do you remember him?

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.760
We fought together as Joi.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.730
Elisugizabe...

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:49.800
When did this monster become 
a colleague of mine?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:54.320
<b>That's mean, senpai. How could you 
forget about me? You'll destroy the world then.</b>

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:53.200
Why are you using these new signs?!

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.320
And that won't destroy the world!

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.610
How could you forget our comrade?

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:02.440
No matter. It's New Year's, so 
you should give him an envelope.

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:03.370
<b>I simply destroy.</b>

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.240
That ain't happening! 
He's so obviously a fake!

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:06.700
<b>Until the beast stops howling.</b>

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.250
And why are you talking like Takasugi?!

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:11.380
You haven't changed at all, Zabethke.

00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:12.380
<b>You may complain now,</b>

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.630
<b>but you'll give me a New 
Year's envelope in the end.</b>

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:18.720
<b>That's what makes you Gintoki-senpai!</b>

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:17.760
Why are you acting like 
this happened before?!

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:18.720
